ous transhepatic biliary drainage</article-title><source>Cardiovasc Intervent Radiol</source><year>2001</year><volume>24</volume><fpage>240</fpage><lpage>244</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11779013</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B14"><label>14</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kato</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Katada</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Anno</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Suzuki</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Ida</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Koga</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Radiation dosimetry at CT fluoroscopy: physician's hand dose and development of needle holders</article-title><source>Radiology</source><year>1996</year><volume>201</volume><fpage>576</fpage><lpage>578</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8888264</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B15"><label>15</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Stoeckelhuber</surname><given-names>BM</given-names></name><name><surname>Leibecke</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Schulz</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Melchert</surname><given-names>UH</given-names></name><name><surname>Bergmann-Koester</surname><given-names>CU</given-names></name><name><surname>Helmberger</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Radiation dose to the radiologist's hand during continuous CT fluoroscopy-guided interventions</article-title><source>Cardiovasc Intervent Radiol</source><year>2005</year><volume>28</volume><fpage>589</fpage><lpage>594</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16132384</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B16"><label>16</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><perso